s clearly worse.","points":["Takes the pawn on g6.","Moves the attacked pawn to safety.","The next best move, 26.Qh3, would drop White's winning chances from 84% to 50% (0.00).","26.hxg6+ saves the attacked pawn and pushes the pawn storm towards the king.","Pushes a pawn towards the Black king, to pry open lines in front of it.","Leaves Black with an isolated pawn on h7: a long-term weakness."]},{"ply":53,"name":"27.Qh3","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"27.Qh3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The queen aims at the e6 pawn, a weak point in front of the Black king.","The next best move, 27.Qc3, would drop White's winning chances from 80% to 50% (0.00).","27.Qh3 threatens Qh7+, with mate in 3.","It threatens Qh7+, with mate in 3, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","Black answers 27…Nxe5, winning a pawn.","After 27…Nxe5 28.Qh7+ Ke8 29.Qh8+ Bf8 30.Bxe5 Qc6, White comes out two pawns up (+4.71)."]},{"ply":55,"name":"28.Qh7+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"28.Qh7+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Skewers the king: when it moves, the bishop on e7 behind it falls.","The queen joins the attack: it now hits 4 squares around the Black king.","The next best move, 28.Re1, would drop White's winning chances from 80% to 59% (+1.02).","28.Qh7+ skewers the king and the bishop on e7.","Gives check, so the reply is forced.","Black answers 28…Ke8."]},{"ply":81,"name":"41.g6","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"41.g6 lets the win slip: 41.Ra5 kept White winning. White's winning chances go from 87% to 56%.","points":["Black answers 41…Bxa3, which takes the rook on a3.","After Bxa3, Black wins 5 points of material within 2 moves.","Better was 41.Ra5 (+5.13), which attacks the b5 pawn, which is undefended."],"better":"41.Ra5 gets the rook out of the way of …Bxa3. Engine line: 41…Kc6 42.g6 Bf8 43.Rxa7 Bxf3 44.Rf7 (+5.13)."},{"ply":82,"name":"41…Ke7","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"41…Ke7 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 44% to 9%.","points":["White answers 42.Rd3: the rook takes the open d-file, aiming at the bishop on d5.","After Rd3, White wins 3 points of material within 4 moves.","Better was 41…Bxa3 (+0.69), which takes the rook on a3."],"better":"41…Bxa3 wins a rook. After 42.g7 Bb2 43.g8=Q Bxe5+ 44.Kh3 Bc7, the pawn promotes on g8 (+0.69)."}],"opening":{"name":"Sicilian Defense: Old Sicilian","eco":"B30","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 11…b6: 22 moves in all, 11 by White and 11 by Black.","Theory runs out after 11…b6: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}